{
 "comment": "Synthetic text for 94S-1888. Each pair holds a `pass` line, where a credential-named field is followed by an identifier that repeats the field name, and the nearest `mask` line that must stay masked: the same field with one condition of the exemption broken. %R% becomes a random letter-and-digit run each test, %H% a random 40-digit hex run, %V% a vendor-shaped token, %W% a short human password, %L% a 90-letter camelCase word that contains the key word and %G% the marker the bundled mock scanner reports, all assembled at run time so no literal here looks like a credential. `masked` is the stdout agent-guard returns and applies to both hosts: Claude rewrites updatedToolOutput, Codex blocks and carries the same text in additionalContext. A `pass` line is left untouched and passes the prompt guard; a `mask` line and every `still_masked` line is rewritten and blocks at the prompt guard. `legacy` is what a `pass` line becomes with AGENT_GUARD_KEY_NAME_REDACT=on.",
